An online shopping company calculates the final order amount based on the purchase amount.

The company provides discounts based on the order value and charges delivery fees based on the same amount.

Your task is to calculate the final amount payable by the customer.
Discount rules
- Order amount below ₹1,000: No discount.
- Order amount from ₹1,000 to ₹2,999: 5% discount.
- Order amount from ₹3,000 to ₹4,999: 10% discount.
- Order amount ₹5,000 and above: 15% discount.
Delivery charges
- Order amount below ₹1,000: ₹100 delivery charge.
- Order amount from ₹1,000 to ₹2,999: ₹50 delivery charge.
- Order amount ₹3,000 and above: Free delivery.

Example 1

Input:
800


Output:
Original Amount = 800.00
Discount = 0.00
Delivery Charge = 100.00
Final Amount = 900.00





import java.util.*;
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
	    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
	    int p = sc.nextInt();
	        double dis = 0;
	        double del = 0;
	        double total = 0;
	    if(p<1000){
	         dis = 0;
	         del = 100;
	         total = p - dis + del;
	        //System.out.printf("Rs.%.2f",total);
	    }else if(p>=1000 && p<3000){
	         dis = p * 5.0/100;
	         del = 50;
	         total = p - dis + del;
	    }else if(p>=3000 && p<5000){
	       
	         dis = p * 10.0/100;
	         del = 0;
	         total = p - dis + del;
	    }else if(p>=5000){
	         dis = p * 15.0/100;
	         del = 0;
	         total = p - dis + del;
	    }else{
	        System.out.printf("Invalid");
	    }
	    System.out.println("Original amount =" +p);
	    System.out.println("Discount =" +dis);
	    System.out.println("Delivery Charge =" +del);
	    System.out.println("Final Price " +total);
	    
	    
		
	}
}
